      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T05:56:19Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(2d): rest machining on the 2D Adaptive from the previous operations\n\nThe 2D Adaptive operation has the rest group. With the group on, the\noperation cuts only what the earlier operations of the setup left. The\nstock that they leave is read at every cut depth (#2033) and goes to the\nrest Adaptive planner (#2031) through\nmachining2d::rest_adaptive_previous. Each plunge stands where that stock\nproves the whole cutter clear.\n\nRefused by name: an entered previous tool, no stock ahead, a roughing\npass that stops above the floor, the Trochoidal method, arc turns, a\ntilt. The group rides EditOperationParams (undo and redo), the project\nkey rest and the MCP edit_operation parameter. Off is the default, and\nan operation without the group keeps its stamp.\n\nStacked on #2822.\n\nFixes #1446\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
